  "body": "Local disk exhaustion prevented qualification of the latest iOS artifact. Add an opt-in hosted macOS journey to the existing interaction workflow: it validates an immutable application SHA, requires an exact native source-tree match, verifies and installs the original simulator artifact, builds the real backend with Stack, and runs the existing HTTP/native tests against disposable PostgreSQL 17. Production credentials and services are never used; only synthetic screenshots are uploaded.\n\nCorrect the release evidence so earlier iOS passes are not presented as qualification of newer artifacts. Record the independent approval and verified App Store Connect access.\n\nValidation: workflow YAML and every shell step parse; specification inventory generation/check and three inventory tests pass. Hosted iOS qualification is running against approved application 0a5653dc349f9faaf237a521aa50016a2fb1d6d9 and simulator run 36519753119.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #470 to preserve its fresh approval. Retarget to main after #470 merges; do not merge this into #470 before release qualification. There are no application or migration changes.\n",
